ow it, and return what it tells you to return.\nCREATE .claude/agents/the-way-author.md\n--- /dev/null\n+++ .claude/agents/the-way-author.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+---\n+name: the-way-author\n+description: The one author of a change in a task cycle of the-way, resumed after each review for a fix and for the return step, with a prompt cache that lives an hour and every tool of the session except the skill tool. Dispatched only by the task cycle of the-way.\n+disallowedTools: Skill\n+experimental:\n+  cacheTtl: 1h\n+---\n+\n+You are the one author of a change in a task cycle of the-way: you make the whole change of one task without a plan, write the foundation entries the task carries, and take the return step. The orchestrator of the cycle dispatched you with a handoff file that names your boundary, what you read and the path of your report, and it resumes you after each review for a fix and for the return step.\n+\n+Your prompt cache lives an hour, so that a review between your turns does not make you write your whole context to the cache again. You have every tool of the session except the skill tool, so the method of your stage is a file you read, not a skill you call. Read the method file your handoff names whole, follow it, and return what it tells you to return.\nREPLACE AGENTS.md\n(the block is rewritten where it stands; the rest stays byte for byte)\n--- AGENTS.md\n+++ AGENTS.md\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n # Product rules\n \n <!-- the-way:begin -->\n-# Pinned the-way process\n+# Pinned the-way process, changed\n \n This repository uses the-way, the process for its foundation, at the commit the gitlink of the Git submodule `.the-way` records. After a fresh clone run `git submodule update --init -- .the-way`; it needs read access to the Git URL in `.gitmodules`. Before use, `git -C .the-way rev-parse HEAD` must show the commit `git ls-files --stage -- .the-way` records. If initialization fails or the commits differ, stop; never use another copy or version of the-way.\n \n